From 9876102085a389d2977765c47c1f341dc1d015c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:10:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] perf(sim): B2 G1 traffic: every phase in pieces, honest
 cost model
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TrafficSystem's phases run as pieces of about INFRA_PIECE_COLD_MS /
INFRA_PIECE_MS estimated warm ms (docs/dev/B2_DESIGN.md §3). A phase state
returns CONT while it has more pieces; sub-stage cursors live in fields; the
whole-state methods the tests call (prep, prepTransit, rebuildGraphs,
roundSearch, roundMatch, poolRemaining, inbound, roundFlows, ...) stay as
loops over the same pieces. Uninterrupted results are unchanged byte for
byte (frozen-original test at three piece scales).

- graph rebuild (decided once per cycle, cancelled by a sync rebuild) runs in
  GraphBuildRun stages; prep / prepTransit build into back buffers from a
  pass-start BuildingSnapshot and publish in one piece (.set / swap with the
  original growth policies); transport-building marks during the scan go to
  a private set (R2).
- searches use RoadSearchRun / TransitSearchRun with private bucket queues,
  so cross-system queries between pieces change nothing (R8); accumulate /
  commit / commitK go by settle-order ranges.
- every external output (traffic, congestion, parking, commute, stop maps,
  bus / ferry / truck rasters, flags, events, save precompute) changes in one
  piece per cycle (R7 / R4); final takes iter++ and the ramp MSA weight in
  its first piece (R1); every cursor resets at cycle end, init and load.
- cost(): one TC table of warm µs per unit + a per-piece fixed cost; each
  piece's estimate mirrors its chunk; stepName names the piece.
- params: provisional INFRA_DAY_BUDGET 5.3 / INFRA_DAY_CARRY 1.0 /
  CREDIT_FLOOR 6.5 (pre-B2 3.2 / 0.6 / 4, scaled by the 1.65 unit change;
  G4 sets the final values).
- tests: frozen traffic 'cities' compares city + traffic at every phase
  transition at production, tiny (one unit per piece) and small piece
  scales (no stepCost equality); b2Pieces traffic tests (one go = production
  = tiny = random pieces across edits, R8 queries between pieces, R7 one
  change per phase visit, R9 mid-cycle save loads idle, two cities
  interleaved, piece estimates within budget); roadTransitSearchSim shadows
  the resumable runs with the wasm kernels; perf P0-15 utilisation
  re-baselined to <= 0.985 (finer pieces fill the day budget closer; B:
  0.869, here 0.961) and traffic's max estimated step <= 1.0.

